WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.440
- All right, there's always
something on social media

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.560
that can bring your day a little extra joy

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.420
and I am always here to share the best,

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:07.643
this is What I'm Liking.

00:00:07.643 --> 00:00:09.692
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.692 --> 00:00:10.870
(audience applauding)

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.640
Going under the knife can
be terrifying for anyone

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.180
but especially children,

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.300
it's like a whole world of unknowns.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.400
So for three decades of pediatric surgeon

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.220
in Akron, Ohio has been
helping children get through

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.770
the fear and anxiety of the experience

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:26.680
all through the wonder of art.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.590
Dr. Bob Parry, hand draws
colorful characters and pictures

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:33.850
and turns them into bandages
to brighten the kids' spirits,

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:35.460
when they awake from surgery.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.030
We have Dr. Parry on the
line right now watching

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.850
on WKYC 3 at 11:00 AM.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.683
Dr. Parry,

00:00:42.949 --> 00:00:43.782
hello.

00:00:43.782 --> 00:00:44.615
(audience applauding)

00:00:44.615 --> 00:00:45.980
- Hey Kelly, how are you?

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.080
- I am so much better
now that you're here,

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.540
so how did you come up with this idea?

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.740
- Well, I have to tell you

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:54.630
it wasn't my idea originally
where I was training

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.550
in the early nineties, but
that's the Naval Hospital,

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:00.020
one of my mentors in pediatric surgery,

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:04.450
he used to cut out sharks for
boys and the hearts for girls.

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:05.970
The kids just loved it,

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.530
you could see they really enjoyed it

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:10.240
and as I went on to my
practice without ado,

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:11.180
you know, through fellowship,

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:12.880
I was actually out in Los Angeles there

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.570
and kept going, did
more and more drawings,

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.150
and it just kinda took off from there.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:19.790
I was thinking the other
day, the past 30 years,

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:23.180
probably 10,000 of these
bandages, I've done over time,

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.817
basically every kid I've operated on.

00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:27.900
- That is so cool,

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.700
well you say this isn't
just about helping kids

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.460
after surgery but before as well, right?

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.800
- Yeah, actually, you know, honestly,

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:37.010
before is even better,

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:38.560
we get kids sometimes
that have heard about it

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.847
and they'll come in, they have ideas of,

00:01:39.847 --> 00:01:41.750
"I want this on my bandage."

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.940
Other times they wanna really any idea,

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:45.817
then the moms and dads
get excited and they go,

00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:47.267
"Oh, what about your dog?"

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:49.500
"Your favorite cartoon
character you love."

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.600
And it kinda distracts them completely

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.370
from the thought of surgery,

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:55.660
everybody, the parents, the child,

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:58.340
you know, the technical side
of the surgery is a little,

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.370
you know, it's obviously
frightening in that time

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.570
before you go to the operating room,

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:02.960
they're all quite nervous

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.610
and suddenly this is
just a huge distraction,

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:09.330
they all get excited and
honestly, even when they wake up,

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:10.787
you know, they're trying
to look at their bandage.

00:02:10.787 --> 00:02:11.620
"Well, what did I get?"

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:12.453
"What happened?"

00:02:12.453 --> 00:02:15.890
And it makes it a really nice transition,

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:18.100
and for me, honestly, it's rewarding

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.930
'cause the technical side of surgery,

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:23.890
is just hard for anyone
to really understand.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:25.630
And this gives me the ability to give

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.980
a little, you know,
personal piece of myself

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.760
that they can relate to a
little compassionately humanity

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.970
that's less than the
cold element of surgery

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:34.530
and it's just fun.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.160
- Well, I mean, honestly,
I was gonna bring that up

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.550
but it's an amazing thing that
you're able to heal people

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.760
and help people in the way
that you do as a doctor,

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.260
but it's an even cooler thing
that you take that extra step

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.550
in being so compassionate

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.330
in a time that's so
frightening for the kids,

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:48.410
their families, everybody.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.790
So thank you so much, all right.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:55.790
I'm liking your posts now, Dr.
Parry and that's not all man.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:57.390
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:58.900
the go to pen at the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.970
wants to honor ultimate
overachievers just like you, man.

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:04.050
So they're gonna be using
their G-2 gelling pen

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.015
to write you a check
for a thousand dollars.

00:03:06.015 --> 00:03:08.423
(audience cheering)

00:03:08.423 --> 00:03:09.790
Yeah, all right,

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.320
well thank you so much.
- Thank you so much,

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.170
that's wonderful.

